From 8c94571da008c0a082635b32888d9cd58becb371 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: littlemex <littlemex@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 17:29:18 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(mvp): stop leaking Anthropic-shaped cache keys into
 chat/completions usage

THE GAP

`/v1/chat/completions` serves both GPT-family and Claude-family models
behind one OpenAI-shaped wire contract. The GPT-family path passes its
upstream usage block through untranslated, already in the correct OpenAI
shape. The Claude-family path (Converse-backed) builds its usage block from
scratch and put the two cache legs at the top level, spelled the Anthropic
way (`cache_read_input_tokens` / `cache_creation_input_tokens`) -- keys the
OpenAI Chat Completions `usage` schema does not define at all.

OBSERVED

vLLM Semantic Router 0.4.0 decodes an upstream chat/completions response
strictly and rejects an unknown field outright: `field "usage": unknown
field "cache_read_input_tokens"`, surfaced to its own caller as a 502 "The
selected model returned an invalid response". Every claude-* call routed
through it over this endpoint failed this way; qwen/nemotron calls over the
same endpoint did not, because neither model reports a cache leg, so the
unknown field was never present for them to reject.

THE FIX

The Converse-backed usage block now nests both cache legs under
`prompt_tokens_details` (`{"cached_tokens": ..., "cache_write_tokens":
...}`) -- the same nesting `mvp._openai_transport.extract_cache_usage`
already reads off a GPT-served response's own usage block, so a caller does
not need a second parser depending on which family served the request. The
whole `prompt_tokens_details` key is omitted, not emitted with nulls, when
neither leg was reported, matching how the two legs were already handled
individually. `prompt_tokens` / `total_tokens` still exclude both cache legs
and that is left as a documented divergence from the official OpenAI
meaning (where `cached_tokens` is a subset of `prompt_tokens`, not
additive) rather than folded in, since changing it would change a number
every existing client already reads for cost math -- out of scope for an
interop-shape fix. `/v1/messages` (the native Anthropic wire format) is
unaffected and keeps its own top-level keys, which are correct there.

Any client that was reading the old top-level `cache_read_input_tokens` /
`cache_creation_input_tokens` keys off `/v1/chat/completions` specifically
(never `/v1/messages`) must move to `usage.prompt_tokens_details
.cached_tokens` / `.cache_write_tokens`.

Updated `tests/test_chat_completions_billing_contract.py`'s existing C8.4
assertions to the new nesting, and added two regression tests (streaming and
non-streaming) pinning that the old top-level keys never reappear on a
response that reports both cache legs.

Delete this patch once it is upstream: when a Converse-backed
`/v1/chat/completions` response reports its cache legs nested under
`usage.prompt_tokens_details` instead of the top-level
`cache_read_input_tokens` / `cache_creation_input_tokens` keys, on the
pinned commit.
